SUMMARY:Grassy Narrows and Indigenous Rights: 150 Years of Resistance - by
  Showing Up for Racial Justice Toronto
LOCATION:Virtual
DESCRIPTION:More info: https://tinyurl.com/GrassyWebinar2026\n\nHosted by
  Showing Up for Racial Justice Toronto
  (https://www.surjtoronto.com/)\n\nWith Chrissy Isaacs and youth from
  Grassy Narrows First Nation. Grassy Narrows has been suffering from
  mercury poisoning from water pollution since the 1960s. They've also been
  a beacon of resistance\, maintaining the longest-running blockade in
  Canadian history\, and fostering Indigenous resistance across Turtle
  Island. Come meet the generations at the frontline of these fights.
END:VEVENT
